<title>JAPAN: M'shita Elec says investment not only based on EMU.</title>
<headline>M'shita Elec says investment not only based on EMU.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Matsushita Electric Industrial Co Ltd said on Friday that the issue of a proposed single currency in Europe is not the only factor it takes into account when making its investment decisions in the region.</p>
<p>&quot;The proposed single currency is merely one factor among many. It would not be enough on its own to influence investment decisions one way or another,&quot; Seinosuke Kuraku, a company director and a member of the board, said in a statement.</p>
<p>He said the company based its investment decisions on a whole host of factors, including the availability of skilled workers, transport links, language and the attitude of the local community.</p>
</text>
